                        <seg type="rubrication">Names of holy persons (name of St Mary in <ref target="#ms_i1.4"/> and <ref target="#ms_i1.5"/>);
                           titles and numbers of the Psalms, Canticles and Song of Songs; title of <ref target="#ms_i1.4"/> and <ref target="#ms_i1.5"/>; incipit of the daily readings of <ref target="#ms_i1.4"/>; 
                           name and traditional interpretation of the Hebrew letters in <ref target="#ms_i1.1">Text 1.1, Psalm 118</ref>; letter <foreign xml:lang="gez">ስ</foreign> in the word <foreign xml:lang="gez">እስመ፡</foreign>
                           in <ref target="#ms_i1.1">Text 1.1, Psalm 135</ref>; letters <foreign xml:lang="gez">ባ</foreign> and <foreign xml:lang="gez">ክ</foreign> of the word <foreign xml:lang="gez">ይባርክዎ፡</foreign> in <ref target="#ms_i1.1">Text 1.1, Psalm 150</ref> and in <ref target="#ms_i1.2">Text 1.2, Canticle 10</ref>;
                          refrains of <ref target="#ms_i1.4"/> and <ref target="#ms_i1.5"/>(one or two initial words or their abbreviations); elements of the punctuation marks and text dividers; Ethiopic numerals or their elements. A few lines on the
                          opening page of <ref target="#ms_i1.1"/>; two lines on the opening page of <ref target="#ms_i1.2"/> and <ref target="#ms_i1.3"/>; two groups of lines in <ref target="#ms_i1.4"/></seg>
